    "morning": ["Hansom cabs clatter through the streets", "Newsboys cry the morning headlines", "Coal smoke hangs low over the rooftops", "The fog lifts reluctantly from the river"],
    "afternoon": ["Pale sunlight struggles through overcast skies", "Ladies promenade in Hyde Park", "The clamour of Covent Garden fills the air", "Church bells chime the hour"],
    "evening": ["Gas lamps hiss to life along the Embankment", "Theatre crowds gather in the West End", "The fog rolls in thick from the river", "Shadows pool in narrow alleyways"],
    "night": ["London belongs to those who prowl its darker streets", "A distant scream echoes and is swallowed by fog", "Gaslight barely penetrates the murk", "Something moves in the shadows between streetlamps"],
    "midnight": ["The witching hour settles over the city", "Only the night soil men and their carts stir", "An unnatural silence grips the streets", "The fog seems almost alive, pressing against windows"]
  },

